I fixed items 1 and 2 of #1052 and committed as d2f81336 (Part of #1052). I posted a comment on #1052 naming both as fixed with the sha, and saying item 3 is still open.

Measured before the fix: in a fresh repo with system_file = "sp" in .yoyo.toml and sp a FIFO, both --print-system-prompt and -p hung until timeout 10 killed them (exit 124). I also probed item 2, which had only been found by reading the code: a FIFO at yoyo-session.json hangs --continue -p the same way.

Change: both reads now go through non_regular_read::read_regular_to_string, the reader #1047 already uses. In src/cli.rs that's a call swap (net +1 line, inside the size-gate headroom). In src/main.rs there's a new RestoreError::NotRegular variant, and every match on that enum is updated.

After the fix: item 1 now fails in 0.007s, and item 2 finishes in 0.2s.

Where I went against the plan, and why: the plan said a FIFO system_file should warn and carry on "as if the file weren't there". But today a missing system_file is a hard error (it names the file and exits 1), so those two instructions conflict. I sent the FIFO down that same error path. Carrying on would run the session under a system prompt the config didn't ask for. For --continue, a FIFO gets a yellow warning that gives the reason, rather than the dim "no previous session found", because a FIFO isn't a missing session. --continue-strict exits 1. A missing file behaves exactly as before on both, and a near-miss test pins that. --system-file <path> on the command line is untouched, as #1052 asked.

Tests (`tests/config_fifo.rs`): four new tests. Two check that a FIFO doesn't hang (item 1, and item 2 with both --continue and --continue-strict). Two near-misses check that a regular system_file is still read and a missing session file still gives the old message. Both FIFO tests failed by hitting the deadline before the swap.

Positive control: in one command, I reverted the cli.rs swap, ran the suite and restored the file. Only fifo_config_system_file_does_not_hang_and_is_named failed, by deadline.

Checks: cargo fmt --check, clippy -D warnings, build and the full cargo test all pass. I added a Day-233 note to the existing #1047 entry in ARCHITECTURE.md. Item 3 (the write_file diff preview in `src/prompt.rs`) is not part of this task.
